# Migrate icon reconstruction and platform export to the migration boundary

Preserve the useful cross-platform icon pipeline while replacing only its giant
generated-Rust reconstruction representation. The durable reconstruction plan is
text data owned by `src/migration/icon/`, and local authored/recovered SVGs remain
ignored evidence rather than distributable repository content.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Keep exact root `Simpsons.ico` mandatory in the lawful source manifest and
  keep `uninst.ico` optional for the game installation.
- [x] Recover the seven SVG assets from the pre-migration authenticated transform
  into local `src/migration/icon/assets/` evidence before replacing the old
  representation; keep that directory ignored by Git.
- [ ] Make `game/Simpsons.ico` the sole icon reconstruction input. `uninst.ico`
  must not participate in icon authoring, replay, or generated platform output.
- [ ] Use the generic Rust function at `src/foundation/algorithm/` to record and
  replay `src/migration/icon/icon_algorithm.txt`; do not generate source code as
  reconstruction data.
- [ ] Preserve the useful SVG renderer, platform profiles, and Windows, macOS,
  Linux, Android, and iOS export behavior under `src/migration/icon/` rather
  than deleting it.
- [ ] Keep `src/migration/icon/assets/` and `src/migration/icon/out/` ignored;
  never commit the authored/recovered SVGs or generated platform icon products.
- [ ] Replay `icon_algorithm.txt` from only lawful `Simpsons.ico` evidence and
  prove all seven local SVG outputs are byte-identical to the recovered oracle.
- [ ] Keep `src/unreal/icon/` retired after parity is proven; icon migration and
  export ownership belongs only to `src/migration/icon/`.
- [ ] Remove the temporary algorithm reference directory only after generic
  algorithm parity and icon exporter preservation are both complete.

## Evidence

The recovered local tree contains `android.svg`, `ios.svg`, `macos-linux.svg`,
`windows-linux.svg`, and three `master/*.svg` files. Those files contain
copyrighted/trademarked visual material and are intentionally ignored local
oracle evidence; they must not be committed or pushed.

The legacy MVP selected `game/*.ico`, which accidentally admitted `uninst.ico`.
That behavior is a migration bug, not a requirement. The replacement binds icon
reconstruction exclusively to `game/Simpsons.ico` while the general source
manifest may continue to recognize `uninst.ico` as optional installation
material.
